    {
      "end": "00:00:13.900",
      "start": "00:00:00.000",
      "text": " Hello, I'm Dr. Steven Steiner."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:18.633",
      "start": "00:00:13.900",
      "text": " We're here at the dry Arizona desert demonstrating the water repelling properties of hydrophobic"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:20.433",
      "start": "00:00:18.633",
      "text": " silica aerogel."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:27.433",
      "start": "00:00:20.433",
      "text": " I'm going to coat my hands withromera aerogel particles made by Cabinerogell."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:38.633",
      "start": "00:00:27.433",
      "text": " And this will put a hydrophobic coating over my hands so that when I place them in the"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:42.733",
      "start": "00:00:38.633",
      "text": " water they come out dry."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:56.733",
      "start": "00:00:43.733",
      "text": " And in fact, when I place my hands under the water you can see a reflection looks quite strange."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:03.733",
      "start": "00:00:56.733",
      "text": " And if I put water on my hands it beads off."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:06.733",
      "start": "00:01:03.733",
      "text": " And this property is called hydrophobicity."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:13.000",
      "start": "00:01:07.733",
      "text": " It's introduced by changing the hydroxyl groups on the backbone of the silica aerogel"
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:20.733",
